+\section{Claim Boundary}
+EchoForge is narrower than a measured radar collection. It publishes public-proxy signatures, detector-facing products, code, configuration, evidence manifests, and paper figures. It does not publish raw generated arrays or measured raw files in Git. The paper-facing positive class is \emph{fixed-wing pusher-prop public proxy}. Repository-compatible legacy identifiers may still appear in generated artifacts, but no measured Iranian-drone radar signature, route model, payload model, deployment geometry, proprietary clutter-rejection behavior, fielded-sensor parity, or classified fidelity is claimed.
+
+\section{End-to-End Data Processing}
+Figure~\ref{fig:dataprocessing} is the reviewer-facing processing trace. EchoForge samples scenario groups, expands each group into take-up, climb, and cruise records, generates radar/cue products, exports denylisted detector views, trains/calibrates on train/CV only, writes the EI selection lock, and scores the holdout once.
