+\section{Engineered Intelligence}
+Engineered Intelligence is the paper's novel lane. EI uses autonomous search over decomposed algorithm families: radar, acoustic, passive-RF, transport/geometry, and fusion-context score components. It evolves sparse nonnegative component weights and fits a monotone geodesic-odds calibrator on train/CV rows only, writes \texttt{selection\_lock.json}, and scores the blind holdout once.
+
+\begin{table}[t]
+  \caption{EI Candidate Discovery and Locked Scoring Algorithm}
+  \label{tab:eialgorithm}
+  \centering
+  \small
+  \begin{tabular}{@{}rp{0.78\columnwidth}@{}}
+    \toprule
+    Step & Operation \\
+    \midrule
+    1 & Read train/CV detector-view scores after labels, group IDs, split keys, time locks, and audit headers are removed. \\
+    2 & Decompose the problem into radar, acoustic, passive-RF, transport/geometry, and fusion-context score families. \\
+    3 & Evolve candidate sparse nonnegative weight vectors on train/CV objective functions. \\
+    4 & Fit monotone geodesic-odds calibration and threshold policy without holdout rows. \\
+    5 & Write the selection lock with component IDs, weights, calibrator, and threshold source. \\
+    6 & Score the blind holdout once and emit KPI, calibration, false-alarm, and leakage evidence. \\
+    \bottomrule
+  \end{tabular}
+\end{table}
+
