+\section{Conclusion}
+EchoForge demonstrates a strict-open path for low-altitude UAS radar and multimodal sensing studies. The central result is simple: EI improves LCB95 Recall@$\leq$1\%FPR from 0.083 to 0.699 over accepted prior fusion, a \kpigain{+742\%} relative gain, while cutting selected-threshold false positives from 49 to 1. The result is useful because it is auditable and bounded. It is not useful as a measured-platform claim, and the paper does not ask the reader to treat it that way.
+
